# Gem TD — core conventions

## Docs path (required lookup)

Canonical docs: `E:\Projects\Docs\project-docs\Unity\unity-gem-td`

- Design: `GDD.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `UI-SPEC.md`
- Plans/status: `planning/`
- Superpowers / SDD ledger: `planning/sdd/` (`progress.md`, task briefs/reports)

**Always read the docs repo** when resuming work, locking designs, or answering “what’s decided / what’s next.” Do not assume absence because the file is not in this Unity workspace. **Phase 2 is closed** (merged PR #3) — do not execute historical `phase2-*` / PR6 plans. Proof-aura combat apply is in. Living work is Phase 3 polish on the current 29-tower set (VFX / sounds / feel). Do not import new towers until `planning/handoff.md` is unfrozen.

**Do not use Notion.** The July 2026 Gem TD Notion tree is retired. Canon is markdown in the docs repo (`HOME.md`).

**Never** create design docs, plans, or `.superpowers/` / SDD scratch inside this game repo. If a skill defaults to `<repo>/.superpowers/sdd`, redirect writes to `…/unity-gem-td/planning/sdd/`.

## Lookup order

Docs repo (absolute path) → SCE (`user-sce`) → Context7 → web. If SCE lacked info that exists only in the docs repo, say what to index.

**SCE query:** search `unity-gem-td`. Do not search “Gem TD” — SCE does not retrieve this tree under that name. Index `Unity/unity-gem-td` in the docs repo if SCE should cover it.

## Pushback

When a suggestion is suboptimal: (1) acknowledge goal (2) why not (3) better option (4) why better (5) when to revisit.

## Engineering

- No gameplay reflection (`Activator`, attribute scan, string→type).
- ScriptableObject data; plain C# logic; thin views.
- Object pools for enemies/projectiles/pops.
- No `System.Linq` in combat ticks — use `for` / reused lists.
- Git: feature branch + PR into protected `main` only.
- Never `git commit` or `git push` unless the user explicitly asks.
- Same-prefab components: inspector `[SerializeField]` refs. No `AddComponent` / `GetComponent` (incl. children) in `Awake`/`Start` for those. See `gem-td-ui.mdc`.

## Conventional TD shell (Bloons-first)

Unique fantasy = gems/sockets (+ map expansion). For place / select / sell / waves / hotkeys / cancel / previews: check **Bloons TD 5/6 first**, match unless docs override. **No** Bloons Upgrade button — see `gem-td-bloons-mechanics.mdc`.

